1	# SemaphoreUI MCP Server
2	
3	A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that connects AI assistants to [SemaphoreUI](https://semaphoreui.com/) - enabling natural language control of Ansible automation.
4	
5	![demo](images/semaphore-mcp-rawoutput.gif)
6	
7	## Quick Start
8	
9	### Prerequisites
10	
11	- Docker (or Podman)
12	- A running SemaphoreUI instance with an API token
13	- Claude Desktop or Claude Code (or another MCP client)
14	- Node.js (for Claude Desktop only - required for `mcp-remote`)
15	
16	### 1. Get a SemaphoreUI API Token
17	
18	1. Login to your SemaphoreUI instance
19	2. Go to User Settings
20	3. Generate a new API token
21	
22	### 2. Run the MCP Server
23	
24	```bash
25	docker run -d --name semaphore-mcp \
26	  --network host \
27	  -e SEMAPHORE_URL=http://localhost:3000 \
28	  -e SEMAPHORE_API_TOKEN=your-token-here \
29	  -e MCP_PORT=8500 \
30	  ghcr.io/cloin/semaphore-mcp:latest
31	```
32	
33	> **Note:** `SEMAPHORE_URL` is where the MCP server connects to SemaphoreUI. `MCP_PORT` is where the MCP server listens for client connections (Claude Desktop/Code). Use this port in your client configuration below.
34	
35	### 3a. Configure Claude Desktop
36	
37	Claude Desktop requires the `mcp-remote` proxy to connect to HTTP-based MCP servers. This requires Node.js to be installed (`npx` comes with npm).
38	
39	Edit your config file:
40	- **macOS**: `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`
41	- **Windows**: `%APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json`
42	- **Linux**: `~/.config/claude-desktop/claude_desktop_config.json`
43	
44	```json
45	{
46	  "mcpServers": {
47	    "semaphore": {
48	      "command": "npx",
49	      "args": ["mcp-remote", "http://127.0.0.1:8500/mcp"]
50	    }
51	  }
52	}
53	```
54	
55	### 3b. Configure Claude Code
56	
57	Claude Code supports remote MCP servers directly:
58	
59	```bash
60	claude mcp add --transport http semaphore http://127.0.0.1:8500/mcp
61	```
62	
63	Verify it's configured:
64	
65	```bash
66	claude mcp list
67	```
68	
69	### 4. Test It
70	
71	Restart Claude Desktop and try:
72	
73	> "List all projects in SemaphoreUI"
74	
75	## Docker Networking
76	
77	The MCP server container needs to reach your SemaphoreUI instance.
78	
79	**SemaphoreUI on the same host:**
80	
81	Use `--network host` so the container can access localhost:
82	
83	```bash
84	docker run -d --name semaphore-mcp \
85	  --network host \
86	  -e SEMAPHORE_URL=http://localhost:3000 \
87	  -e SEMAPHORE_API_TOKEN=your-token \
88	  -e MCP_PORT=8500 \
89	  ghcr.io/cloin/semaphore-mcp:latest
90	```
91	
92	**SemaphoreUI on a different host:**
93	
94	Use the IP or hostname directly (no `--network host` needed):
95	
96	```bash
97	docker run -d --name semaphore-mcp \
98	  -e SEMAPHORE_URL=http://192.168.1.100:3000 \
99	  -e SEMAPHORE_API_TOKEN=your-token \
100	  -p 8500:8000 \
101	  ghcr.io/cloin/semaphore-mcp:latest
102	```
103	
104	For more details, see [Docker's networking documentation](https://docs.docker.com/network/).
105	
106	## Configuration
107	
108	| Variable | Required | Default | Description |
109	|----------|----------|---------|-------------|
110	| `SEMAPHORE_URL` | Yes | - | URL to your SemaphoreUI instance |
111	| `SEMAPHORE_API_TOKEN` | Yes | - | API token from SemaphoreUI |
112	| `MCP_TRANSPORT` | No | `http` | Transport mode: `http` or `stdio` |
113	| `MCP_HOST` | No | `0.0.0.0` | Host to bind to |
114	| `MCP_PORT` | No | `8000` | Port to listen on |
115	
116	## What You Can Do
117	
118	Once connected, you can interact with SemaphoreUI through natural conversation:
119	
120	**Run automation:**
121	> "Run the database backup playbook on production"
122	
123	**Monitor tasks:**
124	> "Show me all failed tasks from the last hour and analyze the errors"
125	
126	**Manage infrastructure:**
127	> "Create a new staging environment with APP_ENV=staging"
128	
129	**Troubleshoot:**
130	> "Get the output from task 42 and tell me why it failed"
131	
132	## Available Tools
133	
134	**Projects:** `list_projects`, `get_project`, `create_project`, `update_project`, `delete_project`
135	
136	**Project backups:** `backup_project`, `restore_project_backup`, `validate_project_backup`, `summarize_project_backup`, `clone_project`
137	
138	**Project users:** `get_project_role`, `list_project_users`, `add_project_user`, `update_project_user`, `remove_project_user`
139	
140	**Views:** `list_views`, `get_view`, `create_view`, `update_view`, `delete_view`
141	
142	**Templates:** `list_templates`, `get_template`, `create_template`, `update_template`, `delete_template`
143	
144	**Schedules:** `list_schedules`, `list_template_schedules`, `get_schedule`, `create_schedule`, `update_schedule`, `set_schedule_active`, `delete_schedule`, `validate_schedule_cron_format`
145	
146	**Tasks:** `list_tasks`, `get_task`, `run_task`, `stop_task`, `get_task_raw_output`, `filter_tasks`, `bulk_stop_tasks`
147	
148	**Analysis:** `analyze_task_failure`, `bulk_analyze_failures`, `get_latest_failed_task`
149	
150	**Events:** `list_events`, `get_last_events`, `list_project_events`, `summarize_project_activity`
151	
152	**Environments:** `list_environments`, `get_environment`, `create_environment`, `update_environment`, `delete_environment`
153	
154	**Inventory:** `list_inventory`, `get_inventory`, `create_inventory`, `update_inventory`, `delete_inventory`
155	
156	**Repositories:** `list_repositories`, `get_repository`, `create_repository`, `update_repository`, `delete_repository`
157	
158	**Access keys:** `list_access_keys`, `get_access_key`, `create_access_key`, `update_access_key`, `delete_access_key`
159	
160	## Troubleshooting
161	
162	**Container won't start or exits immediately:**
163	```bash
164	docker logs semaphore-mcp
165	```
166	
167	**Can't connect to SemaphoreUI from container:**
168	- If SemaphoreUI is on localhost, use `--network host`
169	- Check that the URL is reachable from inside the container
170	- Verify the API token is correct
171	
172	**Claude Desktop not seeing the MCP server:**
173	- Ensure the container is running: `docker ps`
174	- Check the port is accessible: `curl http://127.0.0.1:8500/mcp`
175	- Restart Claude Desktop after config changes
176	
177	**Enable debug logging:**
178	```bash
179	docker run -d --name semaphore-mcp \
180	  --network host \
181	  -e SEMAPHORE_URL=http://localhost:3000 \
182	  -e SEMAPHORE_API_TOKEN=your-token \
183	  -e MCP_PORT=8500 \
184	  -e MCP_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG \
185	  ghcr.io/cloin/semaphore-mcp:latest
186	```
187	
188	## Development
189	
190	For local development and contributing, see [DEVELOPMENT.md](DEVELOPMENT.md).
191	
192	For testing documentation (unit tests, E2E tests, CI/CD), see [TESTING.md](TESTING.md).
193	
194	## Resources
195	
196	- [SemaphoreUI Documentation](https://docs.semaphoreui.com/)
197	- [SemaphoreUI API Reference](https://semaphoreui.com/api-docs/)
198	- [Model Context Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/)
199	- [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/cloin/semaphore-mcp/issues)
200	
201	## License
202	
203	This project is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 - see the [LICENSE](LICENSE) file for details.
204	
205	**Note:** Versions prior to 1.0.0 were released under the MIT License.
206	

